course: dictionary
lesson: 6955
title: Pale: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning, so the words around them are your clues. «She went pale when the dog barked» is about a face: pale means it has less colour than usual, often because someone is frightened or shocked.
explain: Pale can also describe a colour or a light. «The sky was a pale blue» means a light, soft blue, not a strong or dark one. «The moon gave out a pale light» means the light was weak, not bright. Ask yourself: is this about a face, a colour, or a light?
explain: Pale can be a verb too. «Her idea paled in comparison to the winning plan» means her idea seemed less important next to the other one. Beyond the pale is a special phrase that means very bad or not acceptable, so read the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: Pale has several meanings, so check the sentence to find the right one.
fact: «Pale» can describe a face or skin with less colour than usual, often when someone is ill, scared or shocked.
fact: «Pale» can describe a light, soft colour, like «pale blue».
fact: «Pale» can also mean weak, not bright, as in «pale light».
exercise: «She went pale when she heard the news.» What does pale mean here? | A light, soft blue | Bigger than before | *Less colour than usual, often from shock | Very bright and shiny
exercise: «The sky was a pale blue this morning.» What does pale describe? | *A light, soft colour | A bright light | A face | A loud sound
exercise: «The moon gave out a pale light over the field.» Which word tells you the light was weak? | moon | over | field | *pale
test: «Her friend looked pale, would not talk and stared at the floor.» What might this tell you? | She is very happy and excited | The floor is pale | She is painting the floor | *Something may be wrong, and she may need help
test: «Her idea paled in comparison to the winning plan.» What does paled mean here? | Became very ill | *Seemed less important next to something else | Turned bright blue | Got louder and faster
exam: Ella reads «The moth was pale and hard to see on the bark.» What does pale mean here? | Very dark and hidden | *Light in colour, so it was hard to spot | Very loud and noisy | Slow and tired
